      "summary": "Homepage Layout & Content Modules UI",
      "description": "As a \nShopper, \n\n\nI want\n to land on a homepage that presents Zimmermann's seasonal campaigns, featured products, and editorial content in a structured and visually engaging layout, \n\n\nso that\n I can discover new collections, explore the brand, and navigate easily to the products and content I care about.\nThe homepage is composed of the following content modules, in sequence from top to bottom:\nFull-width hero banner\n — A full-bleed image at the top of the page with headline text and a CTA link. Supports full-bleed or padded variants per design.\nFeatured product tiles row\n — A row of 4 product tiles surfacing featured or new-arrival products, each linking to the relevant PDP.\nCampaign/editorial image links row\n — A row of images linking to edits, campaigns, or editorial landing pages.\nShop the Look hero\n — A large-format hero image with a \"Shop the Look\" module positioned to the right, allowing the shopper to explore and navigate to featured products from the look.\nTop categories row\n — A row of category tiles, each with a campaign image, linking to the relevant category PLP.\nEditorial and/or boutique duo\n — A final row containing two equal-width (for desktop) hero images side by side: one linking to an editorial destination and one linking to the boutiques page or store locator.\nThis component can be built with mock content prior to Contentful content model being finalised.",
