      "comments": [
        {
          "id": "13363",
          "body": "Hey \n@Jasmijn Tsang\n - Just reviewing this and some clear ACs, very well written!\n\n\n\n\nAlso a few questions for technical implementation:\nFor the 3 seconds between messages\nThis may need to be revisited given Screen Readers will need to time to get to this and read it out loud. \nif on auto-rotation, the developers need to consider aria labels to notify screen readers of new content\nAre there controls to see multiple pages and to pause/play the auto-rotation? \nThis is generally an accessibility issue with auto playing of carousels - we can likely introduce CSS to stop animations for people with assisted browsers, but also would mean they would need controls and keyboard navigation.\nIf there are multiple messages, does clicking the x icon close all messages, or just the visible one?\nWhen a user clicks the x icon, and the next time they load the page, do these messages come back or is there a cookie/session the devs need to add to ensure the message is not persisted?\nFor this being a Contenful managed element, the team needs to do a \nTechnical Solution Design\n and POC on how we integrate the Business Manager properties to Contenful and call those on the component rendering\nAs this will be a component in the Contenful Studio builder, users can drag-n-drop where this lives on specific pages, but if this is going to live on a PLP and/or PDP or Global across all but Zimmerse, then will likely need a configuration to target specific SFCC Category IDs and Product IDs. ",
          "author": {
            "display_name": "Tim Lavelle",
            "name": "Tim Lavelle",
            "email": "timothy.lavelle@accenture.com",
            "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8/69afd82c-3275-4f1a-82c5-96388b537351/48"
