        {
          "id": "13387",
          "body": "Following up from the thread above — proposing AC updates so this is ready to automate (Gherkin/Zephyr). Rotation timing is now a configurable per-message duration rather than a calculated value, and persistence is cookie-based, so updating 2 and 6 accordingly, plus adding new ACs for category/product targeting and accessibility.\nProposed AC updates:\nGiven the promotional banner is configured with multiple messages, when the page loads, then each message is displayed for a configurable duration (in seconds, set per message in Contentful) before automatically rotating to the next message in the configured sequence.\nGiven a shopper closes the banner by clicking 'x', when they navigate to another page or reload within the same browser session, then a cookie records the closed state and the banner remains hidden site-wide until the cookie expires or is cleared.\n(new)\n Given the promotional banner is placed on a PDP or PLP via Contentful Studio, when it is configured with one or more SFCC Category IDs and/or Product IDs, then the banner is only displayed when the shopper is viewing a matching category or product page.\n(new, draft)\n Given a shopper is navigating via keyboard, when they tab through the page, then the banner's CTA link and close ('x') control each receive visible focus in a logical order and are operable via Enter/Space.\n(new, draft — pending the open question below)\n Given the banner auto-rotates between messages, when a new message displays, then the change is announced to assistive technology via an \naria-live=\"polite\"\n region, without interrupting the user's current screen reader focus.\nOpen question — play/pause:\nClosing the banner removes it entirely for the session, but WCAG 2.2 SC 2.2.2 (Pause, Stop, Hide) requires auto-updating content running longer than 5 seconds to be pausable without being dismissed outright. Do we want a distinct pause-on-hover/focus (a common accessible pattern) or a dedicated pause control, separate from close? This also determines whether AC 9 needs a \"pause on focus/hover\" clause added.\nSquad ownership for test tagging will be confirmed at sprint planning — not blocking on that here.",
          "author": {
            "display_name": "Tim Lavelle",
            "name": "Tim Lavelle",
            "email": "timothy.lavelle@accenture.com",
            "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8/69afd82c-3275-4f1a-82c5-96388b537351/48"
