      "id": "18101",
      "key": "SFCC-88",
      "summary": "Client Services",
      "description": "Epic Summary\n\n\nThis epic enables customer service capability on the SFCC platform, covering the tools and integrations that allow Zimmermann's Client Services team to support customers effectively. It includes the Inside Chat live chat widget, Zendesk integration for customer support ticketing, and Order on Behalf Of (OOBO) functionality allowing authorised CS agents to place orders on a customer's behalf directly from the storefront.\nBusiness Value / Objective\n\n\nZimmermann's Client Services team plays a central role in delivering the brand's elevated client experience — resolving queries, assisting with orders, and supporting VIC customers. This epic ensures CS agents have the tools they need on the new SFCC platform from day one, maintaining service continuity post-migration and supporting Zimmermann's commitment to personalised, high-touch client engagement.\nScope\nIn Scope\nInside Chat live chat widget loading via GTM script injection through the AddingWell container on all storefront pages\nZendesk integration via MuleSoft to support customer service functionality on the storefront — allowing customers to log a support request and CS agents to manage interactions\nOrder on Behalf Of (OOBO): authorised CS agents can search for a customer by email in Business Manager, open an OOBO storefront session, and place an order on the customer's behalf; orders attributed to the customer with an agent identifier and passed to NewStore via MuleSoft\nOOBO session banner displayed on the storefront to confirm the active agent session context\nOOBO access restricted to authorised CS agent roles in Business Manager\nOut of Scope\nInside Chat configuration, routing logic, and widget setup — owned by Zimmermann\nZendesk platform configuration — owned by Zimmermann\nBM role and permission configuration for CS agents — covered in SFCC-23 User Management & Reporting\nOne-off CS promotion code creation — covered in SFCC-87 Promotions\nDependencies\nSFCC-22 SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing — Inside Chat loads via GTM/AddingWell; GTM container must be in place\nSFCC-23 User Management & Reporting — CS agent BM role must be configured before OOBO access can be tested\nMuleSoft — Zendesk integration is via MuleSoft; MuleSoft API must be available for end-to-end testing\nZimmermann — Inside Chat and Zendesk configuration must be completed by Zimmermann before full end-to-end testing can occur\nAssumptions & Constraints\nInside Chat Accenture scope is widget loading only via GTM/AddingWell — all Inside Chat configuration and routing is owned by Zimmermann\nZendesk Accenture scope is the SFCC-side MuleSoft integration only — Zendesk platform setup is owned by Zimmermann\nOOBO is SFCC out-of-the-box functionality; no custom build is anticipated beyond configuration of the CS agent role in Business Manager\nNo designs have been started for this epic; any storefront-facing components (OOBO banner, Zendesk widget) will require design sign-off before build\nPriority:\n Medium\nTarget Release / Sprint:\n TBC",
