      "id": "18100",
      "key": "SFCC-87",
      "summary": "Promotions",
      "description": "Epic Summary\n\n\nThis epic configures and builds Zimmermann's promotions capability on SFCC, covering the promotions engine setup in Business Manager and promotion display across the storefront. It encompasses promotion types, coupon code management, customer group discounts, stacking and exclusion rules, scheduled activation windows, and promotion messaging across the mini-bag, cart, checkout, and order history. The outcome is a fully operational promotions engine that the Site Merchandiser and Client Services teams can manage independently without code deployment.\nBusiness Value / Objective\n\n\nPromotions are a key commercial lever for Zimmermann — driving sale events, rewarding VIC customers, and enabling the Client Services team to resolve customer situations quickly. Migrating promotions from Magento to SFCC's native campaigns and promotions module consolidates this capability within Business Manager, reducing operational complexity and giving the merchandising team direct control over promotion creation, scheduling, and scoping across all 8 regional storefronts.\nScope\nIn Scope\nSFCC Business Manager promotions engine configuration: promotion scoping by storefront, customer group, product/category, and spend threshold\nCoupon code management: single-use unique codes, generic multi-use codes, and bulk CSV import; migration of approximately 8 active Magento promo codes to SFCC at go-live\nMaximum 1 promo code per cart\nPromotion scheduling: start/end dates and times with time-zone awareness per storefront; maximum redemptions configurable per promotion and per customer\nCustomer group pricing and discounts: catalogue-level discounts for VIC Early Access, Gold VIC, Platinum VIC, Advent, and PR/investor groups, visible consistently across PLP, PDP, mini-bag, cart, checkout, recommendations, and wishlist\nPromotion stacking and priority rules: product, order, and shipping promotions stackable with each other; highest discount wins within the same type; customer group discounts excluded from sale items and gift cards\nAuto-applied promotions (e.g. free shipping, customer group discounts) applied silently without code entry\nFree shipping threshold evaluated on post-discount cart total\nRetail Rewards applied after promotion calculation\nOne-off Client Services promotion codes with audit and tracking capability in Business Manager\nPromotion display at line-item and order level across mini-bag, cart, checkout, and order history; applied promotion banner and inline promo code entry with validation feedback on the cart page\nPromotion information passed to NewStore via MuleSoft as part of order placement\nPromotion calculation in the customer's selected ship-to currency across all storefronts\nCart payload including all applied promotions and coupon codes passed to Global-e for international checkout\nOut of Scope\nPrice feed and pricebook sync from AP21 — covered in SFCC-18 Pricing\nGift card and credit note redemption — covered in SFCC-17 Credit Notes & Gift Cards\nRetail Rewards balance retrieval and redemption — covered in SFCC-16 Customer Account & CRM\nBM user role configuration for Client Services — covered in SFCC-23 User Management & Reporting\nGTM/analytics events for promotion interactions — covered in SFCC-22 SEO & Analytics & A/B Testing\nDependencies\nSFCC-18 Pricing — pricebook and customer group price structures must be in place before promotion stacking and exclusion rules can be fully configured\nSFCC-16 Customer Account & CRM — customer group membership is managed via the Omneo integration; group assignment must be available in SFCC before group-specific promotions can be tested end-to-end\nSFCC-17 Credit Notes & Gift Cards — gift card exclusion from customer group discounts requires coordination with the gift card implementation\nMuleSoft / NewStore — promotion data must be passed correctly in the order payload; MuleSoft integration must be available for end-to-end testing\nGlobal-e — cart handoff including promotions and coupon codes must be validated against the Global-e integration for international storefronts\nZimmermann — full list of customer groups and discount rates (Platinum VIC rate, PR/investor rate) must be confirmed before group pricing configuration can be completed\nAssumptions & Constraints\nAll promotions are configured natively in SFCC Business Manager using the Campaigns and Promotions module; no custom promotions engine is required\nPlatinum VIC discount rate and PR/investor group discount rates are TBC — Zimmermann to confirm before those groups can be configured\nFull list of customer groups beyond those currently known is TBC — Zimmermann to provide complete list\nCustomer group discount validation against Global-e international checkout is to be confirmed with the Global-e team\nWhether multiple Retail Rewards per order are supported is TBC — to be confirmed with Zimmermann\nPriority:\n Medium\nTarget Release / Sprint:\n Sprint 4",
