{"result":"{
  "id": "18434",
  "key": "SFCC-238",
  "summary": "Spike: Contentful-to-PWA Kit Product/Category ID Rendering (Hook Integration)",
  "description": "**Objective**\n\nDocument how SFCC Product and Category IDs authored in a Contentful content model are resolved to rendered commerce data in the PWA Kit — specifically which `@salesforce/commerce-sdk-react` hook is called, where that hook lives, and how the ID key passes from the Contentful entry into the hook — so the squad has one confirmed pattern to reuse across every content type that embeds a product or category reference (product spotlights, Shop the Look, PLP inline grid inserts, mega-menu tiles).\n\n**Background**\n\nThe Contentful App for SFCC (Salesforce Commerce Cloud connector) is now installed, letting content authors pick SFCC product/category IDs directly inside Contentful entries. A working single-product bridge already exists in the codebase — `productHero.tsx` and the ShoppableImage hotspots both pass a Contentful `productId` string into `useProduct` — but it was built against a mock space using plain string fields, resolves client-side, and has no category or multi-product equivalent. SFCC-123 (Contentful Integration TSD) documents the page-scoping filter pattern but explicitly leaves reference-resolution / hook-wiring open; this spike closes that gap. Note the existing bridge calls `useProduct` inside leaf components, which conflicts with the container/presentational rule and the SSR-first/LCP mandate — this needs an explicit ruling. Angelo to align with the SFCC-123 owner (Jhoan) and the incoming Contentful squad.\n\n**Tasks**\n\n- Document the existing product-ID → hook bridge (`useProduct` in `productHero.tsx` and `hotspotPopup.tsx`) and the `productId` convention (`SFCC_PRODUCT_ID_FIELD`) as the current-state baseline\n- Determine how the newly-installed Contentful App for SFCC surfaces product/category references (field type and payload shape) and map that to the commerce hook's key parameter\n- Define the confirmed resolution mechanic: which hook per reference type (`useProduct` for products; `useCategory` / `useProductSearch` for the category gap), where it is called (SSR container vs leaf component), and how the ID passes through\n- Reconcile the pattern with the container/presentational rule and the SSR-first / ≤2s p75 mobile LCP budget — rule on client-side hook vs SSR fetch-and-pass-down\n- Cover the reference variants missing today: category references (no bridge exists) and multiple/array product references (single `productId` only)\n- Confirm product name/price ownership (Contentful vs SFCC) to close HPC-001, since the pattern assumes IDs in Contentful and all commerce data resolved from SFCC\n\n**Definition of Done**\n\nA Technical Solution Document (following the official 8-section TSD template) is produced and signed off per Section 8, documenting the confirmed reference-resolution pattern — which hook, where it is called, and how the Contentful ID key is passed — validated for both product and category references and for single and multiple references, reconciled with the SSR-first and container/presentational rules, and sufficient for the squad to build any embedded-reference content type consistently.",
  "status": {
    "name": "Ready for Development",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  }
}"}

