          "body": "The Studio team and Content team do not assign Alt text to product images. We assign them to all other images on the website (content pages, menu image etc), but not for product. This would significantly impact the workflow and would love an AI solution - do we know if Contentful can help with this as part of their AI actions?\nCurrent state: \nAt the moment every image on a PDP, the hero shot, the gallery thumbnails, and any close-ups, carries the same alt text: just the product name. This is automated through M2. \nOn the \nValiant Lingerie Gown in Dark Periwinkle\n, for example, all eight-plus images in the gallery are tagged with the identical \"Valiant Lingerie Gown\". A screen reader user working through that gallery hears the same two words repeated eight times, with no way to tell one image from another. \nIdeal state: \nEvery image of the same product (front view, back view, close-up, colour swatch) needs its own unique alt text. Copying the product title across every shot makes it hard for both search engines and screen reader users to tell products apart. e.g. \nHero/front view: \nalt=\"Zimmermann Valiant Lingerie Gown in Dark Periwinkle, front view on model, fitted lace corset bodice with high stand collar and long sleeves\"\nBack detail: \nalt=\"Back view of the Zimmermann Valiant Lingerie Gown in Dark Periwinkle, showing the keyhole opening and centre back zip\"\nBest practice guidelines for Zimmermann \nproduct image alt text here >>\n (supplied by Sparro)",
