    {
      "id": "17901",
      "key": "SFCC-51",
      "summary": "Promotional Announcement Banner UI",
      "status": {
        "name": "Blocked",
        "category": "In Progress",
        "color": "yellow"
      },
      "issue_type": {
        "name": "Story"
      },
      "labels": [
        "Contentful",
        "DesignDependent",
        "HPC-017"
      ],
      "comments": [
        {
          "id": "13363",
          "body": "Hey \n@Jasmijn Tsang\n - Just reviewing this and some clear ACs, very well written!\n\n\n\n\nAlso a few questions for technical implementation:\nFor the 3 seconds between messages\nThis may need to be revisited given Screen Readers will need to time to get to this and read it out loud. \nif on auto-rotation, the developers need to consider aria labels to notify screen readers of new content\nAre there controls to see multiple pages and to pause/play the auto-rotation? \nThis is generally an accessibility issue with auto playing of carousels - we can likely introduce CSS to stop animations for people with assisted browsers, but also would mean they would need controls and keyboard navigation.\nIf there are multiple messages, does clicking the x icon close all messages, or just the visible one?\nWhen a user clicks the x icon, and the next time they load the page, do these messages come back or is there a cookie/session the devs need to add to ensure the message is not persisted?\nFor this being a Contenful managed element, the team needs to do a \nTechnical Solution Design\n and POC on how we integrate the Business Manager properties to Contenful and call those on the component rendering\nAs this will be a component in the Contenful Studio builder, users can drag-n-drop where this lives on specific pages, but if this is going to live on a PLP and/or PDP or Global across all but Zimmerse, then will likely need a configuration to target specific SFCC Category IDs and Product IDs. ",
          "author": {
            "display_name": "Tim Lavelle",
            "name": "Tim Lavelle",
            "email": "timothy.lavelle@accenture.com",
            "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8/69afd82c-3275-4f1a-82c5-96388b537351/48"
          },
          "created": "2026-07-07T09:14:03.842+1000",
          "updated": "2026-07-07T09:14:03.842+1000"
        },
        {
          "id": "13385",
          "body": "@Tim Lavelle\n Thanks for this review! \n\n\nI’ve asked Dani for some input, and we’ve come to these conclusions: \nRotation time should be configurable and depends on the length of the message. The duration needs to be adjusted to cover the message. So 3 seconds is definitely not fixed, I’ll update that in the AC. \nWith regards to Pause, does the 'x' as Close button not cover the ability that one must be able to stop this rotating element from happening?\nCan confirm ‘x' will close all messages in the banner, not just the one currently displayed. I’ll update AC. \nIf that banner is displayed in any other pages, it will remain closed if the user has used ‘x' to close it already in that session, so we do need to find a way to ensure it’s not persisted. I’ll update AC.\nYes, created spike for that in sprint 1.\n@Marcel Angelo Navarro\n think this one is relevant for the TSD as well. This banner is def currently available on PLP and PDP pages.",
          "author": {
            "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
            "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
            "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
            "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
          },
          "created": "2026-07-09T12:07:49.830+1000",
          "updated": "2026-07-09T12:07:49.830+1000"
        },
        {
          "id": "13386",
          "body": "Changed the AC after sign off - good to check once more on Tuesday with Emma/Rebecca.",
          "author": {
            "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
            "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
            "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
            "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
          },
          "created": "2026-07-09T12:26:28.280+1000",
          "updated": "2026-07-09T12:26:28.280+1000"
        },
        {
          "id": "13387",
          "body": "Following up from the thread above — proposing AC updates so this is ready to automate (Gherkin/Zephyr). Rotation timing is now a configurable per-message duration rather than a calculated value, and persistence is cookie-based, so updating 2 and 6 accordingly, plus adding new ACs for category/product targeting and accessibility.\nProposed AC updates:\nGiven the promotional banner is configured with multiple messages, when the page loads, then each message is displayed for a configurable duration (in seconds, set per message in Contentful) before automatically rotating to the next message in the configured sequence.\nGiven a shopper closes the banner by clicking 'x', when they navigate to another page or reload within the same browser session, then a cookie records the closed state and the banner remains hidden site-wide until the cookie expires or is cleared.\n(new)\n Given the promotional banner is placed on a PDP or PLP via Contentful Studio, when it is configured with one or more SFCC Category IDs and/or Product IDs, then the banner is only displayed when the shopper is viewing a matching category or product page.\n(new, draft)\n Given a shopper is navigating via keyboard, when they tab through the page, then the banner's CTA link and close ('x') control each receive visible focus in a logical order and are operable via Enter/Space.\n(new, draft — pending the open question below)\n Given the banner auto-rotates between messages, when a new message displays, then the change is announced to assistive technology via an \naria-live=\"polite\"\n region, without interrupting the user's current screen reader focus.\nOpen question — play/pause:\nClosing the banner removes it entirely for the session, but WCAG 2.2 SC 2.2.2 (Pause, Stop, Hide) requires auto-updating content running longer than 5 seconds to be pausable without being dismissed outright. Do we want a distinct pause-on-hover/focus (a common accessible pattern) or a dedicated pause control, separate from close? This also determines whether AC 9 needs a \"pause on focus/hover\" clause added.\nSquad ownership for test tagging will be confirmed at sprint planning — not blocking on that here.",
          "author": {
            "display_name": "Tim Lavelle",
            "name": "Tim Lavelle",
            "email": "timothy.lavelle@accenture.com",
            "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/557058:1a7fb05a-783b-4241-a0f1-9a7b046da3a8/69afd82c-3275-4f1a-82c5-96388b537351/48"
          },
          "created": "2026-07-09T12:56:37.971+1000",
          "updated": "2026-07-09T12:56:37.971+1000"
        },
        {
          "id": "13388",
          "body": "Questions for next week’s refinement:\nShowing the banner on PDP/PLP - would it ever be a specific category / product and others not? Or is it: it either shows on all PLPs / all PDPs or none?\nIs the banner global, except on Zimmerse? Can we get some information on the rules - where to show and where not to show, even though we understand it must be flexible - it may impact the way we design it if we can get a bit more info on this\nGet thoughts on having a distinct pause-on-hover or dedicated pause control separate from close for accessibility - see Tim’s comment below.",
          "author": {
            "display_name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
            "name": "Jasmijn Tsang",
            "email": "jasmijn.tsang@accenture.com",
            "avatar_url": "https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d/40fcd533-06f6-4e5b-ba9f-23879e1193f9/48"
