fore we close Blocker #1 as 9?\nSprint-2 content-types table.\n Two of these belong in later sprints: SFCC-67 (Checkout Trust Messaging) sits under the Checkout Flow & Delivery epic, which is Sprint 4, and SFCC-14 (Returns/Refund) is an Epic, which is Sprint 7 - and as you and Tim both noted, we build to a child story, not the epic. Let's remove both rows from the Sprint-2 table and relocate them: SFCC-67 under Sprint 4, SFCC-14 under Sprint 7 (attaching to its child story once it's raised).\nValidate Before Finalising\nSprint-2 content types.\n You rightly flagged these are assumed, not confirmed (SFCC-82, SFCC-190, SFCC-67 defer their model to stories not yet created; none map to an HPC requirement in 04.1.1). \n@Tim Lavelle\n - you'd mentioned running the Sprint-2 authoring approach by Emma and Dani; is that still the plan, and how would you like us to sequence it before we lock the field sets? In the meantime, Jhoan, let's mark the Sprint-2 types provisional.\nMega Menu fields.\n Design-dependent, as you noted - SFCC-96 needs the Figma spec first (it's flagged DesignDependent in Jira). Let's mark those fields provisional pending the design.\nSpikes and To-Dos to Raise (Not Blocking)\nPLP Inline Grid Insert.\n The ID pattern presents the PLP inject as resolved, but Tim flagged we need to confirm we can inject a Contentful item into the SFCC PLP grid without breaking item counts or pagination. There's already a spike for this area - SFCC-238 (Contentful-to-PWA Kit Product/Category ID Rendering) - let's link it here and confirm it covers the pagination/item-count check, and mark the PLP inject \"pending SFCC-238\" in the meantime.\nPDP Accordion, mixed content.\n Tim raised whether the accordion body can pull SFCC content via a simple SFCC var or needs a dedicated component, and you suggested a spike - there's no card for it yet, so let's raise one (or fold it into SFCC-238's scope) and reference it here.\nMRT-apps section.\n As agreed, we'll scratch this - the MRT